! A deliberately desynchronised disassembly listing, as the positive control
! for check-68060-safe.py's sync detection.  The label <desynced> claims
! 0x80000108 and the next instruction begins at 0x8000010a, which is what a
! listing looks like after the decoder has been knocked off boundary -- and in
! that state a real instruction can have been swallowed as another one's
! operand and never listed at all.  The tool must refuse to call this clean.
!
! Kept because a check that has only been run on inputs it passes is a check
! whose failure path is untested, which is the mistake this file exists to
! prevent from recurring.  objdump ignores lines it did not write, so the
! comment markers are harmless.

/tmp/x:     file format elf32-m68k

Disassembly of section .text:

80000100 <good>:
80000100:	4e56 0000      	linkw %fp,#0
80000104:	4e5e           	unlk %fp
80000106:	4e75           	rts

80000108 <desynced>:
8000010a:	4e56 0000      	linkw %fp,#0
8000010e:	4e75           	rts
